%% Device forward (layer 2): one control-source write forwarded from the controller to a member.
%% Index and code mapping: docs/dev/arch-assets.md
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant S as Control source
  participant C as Controller Core
  participant M as Member front door
  participant R as Member Core
  participant N as Member native session store
  S->>C: act {op, args: device target + agent + operation args}
  Note over S,C: Ops gain device target argument · MCP guide/query/act structures stay frozen
  C->>C: resolve (device, agent) · one direct member only
  Note over C,R: Nesting supported · protocol forwarding = false · no transitive dispatch
  alt member offline
    C-->>S: DEVICE_OFFLINE, not sent, next query devices
  else member online
    C->>C: reserve receipt ID and forward record with origin
    C->>M: peer request on LAN mutual TLS or tunnel token
    M->>R: private IPC with peer source
    R->>R: receipt under the same ID
    R->>N: Agent or host op runs natively
    R-->>C: member result
    C->>C: associate member task with controller and originating source
    Note over C,R: Controller branch includes only tasks it dispatched to this member
    Note right of R: Member shows controller as source · own-source tasks stay local
    C-->>S: member result, or uncertain with receipt read
  end
  C->>M: ordinary peer request: events cursor, wait up to 25 s
  M->>R: authenticated peer event read
  R-->>C: bounded task event batch or overflow gap
  opt reconnect or overflow gap
    C->>R: status reads for open bindings only
    R-->>C: observed state, offline remains unconfirmed
  end
  C-->>S: delivery through the existing notification owner
